+entity at `vkq_vr_aim_hand()` UNCONDITIONALLY. So when the fire scheduler switched
+the server's active weapon to the off hand's gun in order to fire it — which is
+exactly what holding the off-hand trigger does — the aim hand kept drawing
+cl.viewent and therefore drew the OTHER hand's weapon, playing its firing
+animation. The off hand drew its own model correctly at the same time, which is why
+the screenshot shows two nailguns. Right-trigger fire looked correct only because
+the right hand is where cl.viewent already lived.
