+derived from the same fact the scheduler acts on — the SERVER's active weapon —
+rather than from the scheduler's own transient ownership. Deriving it from
+STAT_ACTIVEWEAPON is deliberate and is what makes it correct across the round trip:
+cl.viewent's model is built from the server's stats, so anchoring it to the hand
+that holds THAT weapon keeps model and hand consistent in every frame, including
+the ones where the client has already flipped ownership but the server has not yet
+caught up. Anchoring to vkq_vr_fire_owner instead would tear during exactly those
+frames — the frame-skew bug R6 already paid for once in the cross-fire instrument.
